package m07core048wrappers
    provides [checks, expected_vector, observe, case_body, descriptor, context, check, check_ref, expected_check, evidence, observation, failed, test_case]
    uses [text]

/// M07 CORE-048 "bundled wrappers: policy preservation, recovery, error identity".
/// Source: tests/integration/wrap_test.go symbol TestCurrentBundledWrappers.
/// Related fixture: compiler/testdata/current/wrap/main.can plus the raw
/// offline fixtures under compiler/testdata/current/wrap/fixtures
/// (load.json for load, load_timeout.json for settled, assess.json for
/// assess) and the httptest double (Go L36-65: /load modes at L40-53,
/// /systemone judge protocol at L54-61).
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): nested wrapper/recovery policies preserving the
/// selected fixture rows and error identity; the assert-report evidence
/// labels with no live-quality claim and no live requests; the 404
/// grandchild recovery with exactly one load and one judge request; the
/// 429-busy delegation and 503-broken renormalization escaping as one
/// normalized infrastructure failure; the successful-load bypass reaching
/// the checks failure; the wrong emitted local key failing verification;
/// the judge protocol; and the strict-ts leg.
/// The 13-root green pin lives in core-048-roots-green.can; the TFT
/// production process shape lives in core-048-run-shape.can.
/// Variants: 404 (missing/default), 429 busy, 503 broken, success (ok),
/// missing local key (Go L141-184); the optional CAN_TSC strict
/// generated-TypeScript leg (L186-205) is env-gated and recorded
/// blocked, never waived.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE + macOS sandbox-exec; requires
/// can-bun-archive, macos-sandbox-exec. CAN_I17_TOKEN is harness-supplied
/// (Go L90: "test-only"), not an external gate. Logical gates
/// SUITE/DIAG/FAULT and C/R/N/S/A identities bind at P23/QHTTP/QN1; no
/// live run now. Descriptor timeout 120000ms mirrors the Go 2-minute ctx
/// (L27).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23/QHTTP/QN1 unmet).
/// Case bundled/wrap-semantics checks: report-labels, no-live-quality,
/// assert-silence, cached-policy, settled-policy, guarded-policy,
/// recover-404, error-identity, busy-429, broken-503, load-bypass,
/// bypass-identity, wrong-key, judge-protocol, strict-ts, load-count.
/// Facet map (wrap_test.go legs): report-labels pins the assert-report
/// evidence (L125-129: policy-fixture, raw-provider-fixture, real-can,
/// supplied-completion or the test fatals); no-live-quality pins the
/// offline claim (L130-132: "live-quality" must be absent);
/// assert-silence pins the assertion silence (L133-137: loads 0 and
/// batches 0 or "assertions issued live requests" fatals); cached-policy
/// pins the child policy (fixture L23-26: native 404 yields receipt(0),
/// every other status inherits; rows L19-22 absent/busy);
/// settled-policy pins the grandchild policy (fixture L36-40: native 404
/// yields receipt(0), 429 inherits, every other status renormalizes to
/// http::request_failed; rows L30-35 gone/slow/stalled);
/// guarded-policy pins the assess wrapper (fixture L92-97: native 404
/// yields 0.0 and any other status inherits, emitted invalid_answer
/// yields 0.0; rows L88-91 absorbed/missing); recover-404 pins the 404
/// path (L139-149: the default mode recovers through the grandchild with
/// the judge batch succeeding; loads 1 and batches 1, each underlying
/// operation exactly once); error-identity pins the normalized failure
/// (L158: diag carries "can.error.v2:can.std.http@1::request_failed"
/// verbatim); busy-429 pins the busy path (L151-160: 429 delegates
/// grandchild to child to default and escapes normalized); broken-503
/// pins the broken path (L151-160: 503 renormalizes at the grandchild
/// and escapes normalized); load-bypass pins the success path (L162-170:
/// the ok mode bypasses policy untouched so count 7 reaches the receipt
/// assertion instead of any handler); bypass-identity pins the bypass
/// failure (L168: diag carries "checks::failed" and
/// ""identity":"can.error.v2:can.std.checks@1::failed"" verbatim);
/// wrong-key pins the coverage mutation (L172-184: dropping the absorbed
/// row that selects the emitted local key fails the build with
/// "selecting local"); judge-protocol pins the batch request (L57-61:
/// POST with a nonempty Authorization, Content-Type application/json and
/// "model":"jev-latest" in the body; the batch resolves resolved-model);
/// strict-ts pins the optional leg (L186-205: strict tsc over emitted
/// dist TypeScript via CAN_BUN runs if and only if CAN_TSC is set);
/// load-count pins the served count (L53/L162-163: {"count":7} reaches
/// the receipt assertion on the bypass path).
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
